<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Darwin is a 40-year-old man with a provisional diagnosis of cyclic vomiting syndrome who comes for his preventive health visit, six weeks after his three-month review. He has had no vomiting episode since then and no emergency visits this year since starting treatment. He takes amitriptyline 75 mg at bedtime with a dry mouth and mild constipation, and carries his sumatriptan and ondansetron. His cold in May cleared in two weeks without an episode. He walks most days and practices relaxation breathing each evening. He completed the health risk assessment in the waiting room. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic preventive visit, age 40</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Cyclic vomiting syndrome, provisional, on amitriptyline prophylaxis</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Amitriptyline 75 mg at bedtime; sumatriptan nasal spray and ondansetron dissolving tablets for episodes</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No emergency visits or hospital stays since treatment began</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Better than in the winter, in his words</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with his family; works from home; less worried about episodes in company since treatment began</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco and nicotine</td><td>Does not smoke or vape</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One or two glasses of wine a week (AUDIT-C 2)</td></tr><tr><td>Cannabis and other drugs</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 to 45 minutes most days</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular small meals, as advised for his trigger plan</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven to eight hours; mild morning grogginess on amitriptyline</td></tr><tr><td>Home and road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; smoke detectors working; no firearms in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>One long-term partner; no new partners</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

