    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Preventive visit, age 40</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression and alcohol screens negative. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is below 5 percent by the pooled cohort equations, so no statin is indicated. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Cyclic vomiting syndrome, provisional (R11.15)</content>. No episode in six weeks on amitriptyline 75 mg. Dry mouth and mild constipation are tolerable. [S]<list><item>Continue amitriptyline 75 mg at bedtime.</item><item>More fluid and fiber for the constipation.</item><item>Six-month review in about seven weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 also followed every three months on amitriptyline</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>GAD-7 6 six weeks ago, down from 8; repeated every three months</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2; within low-risk limits</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No cannabis or other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Does not smoke or vape</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>116/72 mmHg; recheck yearly from 40</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 178, HDL 58, LDL 102, triglycerides 90 mg/dL; ten-year risk below 5 percent; no statin indicated</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended for adults 35 to 70 with overweight or obesity; BMI 21.7, and glucose was normal in March</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with his consent; no prior result on record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody, and core antibody), drawn before today&apos;s vaccine dose</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No record of a prior series; first dose of the two-dose adjuvanted vaccine given today, second dose in one month</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine due in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; he plans to have this season&apos;s vaccine with the influenza vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Booster about seven years ago; next due in about three years</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Routine catch-up ends at 26; at 40 with no new risk, not recommended after discussion</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 45</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision starts at 55</td></tr><tr><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Discussed; he will choose a health care agent and return the form</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (adjuvanted, two-dose series), dose 1 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month review of the cyclic vomiting plan in about seven weeks. Second hepatitis B dose in one month. HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B results by portal message. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-08: six-month review of response to prophylaxis. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

